<title>SINGAPORE: Haw Par 1996 net profit down 7 pct.</title>
<headline>Haw Par 1996 net profit down 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  32.91 vs   35.44</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	    11.00 vs   11.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	 18.00 vs   19.40</p>
<p>    Turnover		   340.65 vs  325.66</p>
<p>    Investment income	 13.04 vs   21.70</p>
<p>    Other &amp; interest income  5.54 vs    4.07</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  11.06 vs    7.98</p>
<p>    Pretax			48.78 vs   47.67</p>
<p>    Tax			   15.56 vs   14.11</p>
<p>    Minorities		  (9.07)vs   (6.05)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    4.22 vs    1.35</p>
<p>Note - Trading-based Har Par Brothers International Ltd said profit fell because of a drop in investment income and 1995 results included a once-off tax exempt dividend of S$9.2 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
